# Work Memory (Cross-Project)

Canonical store (all projects):

`/Users/thien.nguyen/thiennp.github.io/agents/work-memory/`

## Before any substantive task

1. Read `INDEX.md`
2. Read `mistakes/INDEX.md` (always)
3. Open only matching entries (by project/tags/keywords)
4. Apply relevant **Do / Don't** before acting

Skip only for pure meta chat (thanks, status, short clarification with no implementation).

## After a big enough task

A task is "big enough" if it took multiple steps, hit a blocker, changed process/tooling, or could fail the same way again.

1. Add or update one entry per [SCHEMA.md](../../work-memory/SCHEMA.md)
2. Refresh category `INDEX.md` + root `INDEX.md` + `tags/INDEX.md`
3. Double-check you are not repeating a pinned mistake

Commands: `/work-memory-recall`, `/work-memory-log`, `/work-memory-finish-check`  
Skill: `work-memory`

## Hard rules

- No secrets in memory files
- Prefer short, indexed Markdown over chat dumps
- Project-local rules still win for that repo’s code standards
- Product Knowledge Base / per-repo RAG are separate; do not replace them
